Package: cS
Type: Package
Title: Contaminated Survival Models
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-10-07
Authors@R:
    person("Arno", "Otto", email = "arno.otto@up.ac.za",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6565-2910"))
Description: Density, survival, hazard and random generation functions, and
    maximum likelihood estimation, for the contaminated survival (cS) model.
    The cS model is a two-component mixture in which both components share the
    same reference survival distribution and differ only in the level of the
    hazard: a proportion alpha of the observations belongs to a delayed
    component whose hazard is multiplied by eta in (0, 1). Two members are
    implemented: the contaminated exponential (cE) and the contaminated
    Weibull (cW). Parameters are estimated with the EM algorithm, and the
    mixing weight may depend on concomitant variables through a logistic
    link. Includes the January 2024 Ecuadorian birth registration data used
    in Otto (2026).
